{"name":"Underwater Realm","hex":"#243062","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"underwater","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Beneath the surface of the water; of or pertaining to the region beneath the water surface.","Beneath the water line of a vessel."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["So as to go beneath the surface of the water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/underwater"},{"term":"realm","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A territory or state, as ruled by an absolute authority, especially by a king; a kingdom. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\n\n An otherworldly dimension or domain — magical, ethereal, or otherwise.\n The spiritual state of which God is the head; the Kingdom of Heaven.","An otherworldly dimension or domain — magical, ethereal, or otherwise."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/realm"}],"entries":[{"title":"Underwater environment","blocks":[{"text":"An underwater environment is an environment of, and immersed in, liquid water in a natural or artificial feature, such as an ocean, sea, lake, pond, reservoir, river, canal, or aquifer. Some characteristics of the underwater environment are universal, but many depend on the local situation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Great_Barrier_Reef_snorkeling_18.jpg/330px-Great_Barrier_Reef_snorkeling_18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Underwater_environment","wikidata":"Q3246517"},{"title":"Realm","blocks":[{"text":"A realm is a community or territory over which a sovereign rules. The term is commonly used to describe a monarchical or dynastic state. A realm may also be a subdivision within an empire, if it has its own monarch, e.g. the German Empire."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Realm","wikidata":"Q1250464"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/